open returns the lowest free number: 1
closed number reused first: 1
pipe takes two lowest numbers in order: 1
dup fills the hole left by close: 1
F_DUPFD with minimum 100 lands exactly there: 1
second F_DUPFD with minimum 100 lands one higher: 1
after closing 100 it is handed out again: 1
F_DUPFD with minimum 0 behaves like dup: 1
F_DUPFD_CLOEXEC: new fd cloexec=1, original cloexec=0
F_DUPFD from a cloexec source: cloexec=0
F_DUPFD with negative minimum: 1 EINVAL
after close(0) the next open returns 0: 1
descriptor table back to its starting shape
